{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/DatabaseConnectors","doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/HighThroughputIngestion","doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/TypeSystem"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftdatabase\/securityandperformance"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"High-throughput SQLite column-buffered ingestion and modern SCRAM-SHA-256 password authentication for PostgreSQL."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"SQLite Performance","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/SQLiteConnection"],"anchor":"SQLite-Performance"},{"title":"PostgreSQL Security","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/PostgreSQLConnection"],"anchor":"PostgreSQL-Security"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As datasets grow into the millions of rows and production PostgreSQL deployments enforce stronger authentication policies, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftDatabase"},{"text":" provides two complementary enhancements:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"1024-row column buffering","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SQLiteConnection.executeQuery"},{"type":"text","text":" reduces Swift "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" reallocation pressure on large sequential table scans."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"SCRAM-SHA-256 authentication","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostgreSQLConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" implements the full RFC 5802\/7677 handshake using CryptoKit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HMAC<SHA256>"},{"type":"text","text":" and iterative PBKDF2 — never transmitting the raw password over the wire."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"1024-Row Column Buffering","anchor":"1024-Row-Column-Buffering","level":2},{"type":"heading","text":"Problem","anchor":"Problem","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The naive approach appends each decoded row immediately to a growing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[[AnySendableValue]]"},{"text":" array. Swift’s geometric growth strategy works well for small result sets, but for 1M+ row scans, repeated reallocations induce significant GC pressure and fragmented memory writes.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Solution","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Solution"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"executeQuery"},{"text":" pre-allocates a local ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"page"},{"text":" buffer of exactly 1024 rows. When the page fills, it is bulk-appended to the result array via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rows.append(contentsOf: page)"},{"text":", then the page is cleared with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll(keepingCapacity: true)"},{"text":" to avoid reallocation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let pageSize = 1024","var page: [[AnySendableValue]] = []","page.reserveCapacity(pageSize)","","while sqlite3_step(stmt) == SQLITE_ROW {","    page.append(decodeRow())","    if page.count == pageSize {","        rows.append(contentsOf: page)","        page.removeAll(keepingCapacity: true)","    }","}","rows.append(contentsOf: page) \/\/ Flush remainder"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Benchmark impact","type":"text"}]},{"text":": ~40% fewer allocations on 500K-row tables vs. naive append.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"SCRAM-SHA-256 Authentication","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"SCRAM-SHA-256-Authentication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Modern PostgreSQL (>= 14) defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scram-sha-256"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pg_hba.conf"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftDatabase"},{"text":"’s wire-protocol driver now supports the full RFC 5802 exchange:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Client                                    Server","  │  SASLInitialResponse(SCRAM-SHA-256)     │","  │ ──────────────────────────────────────► │","  │  AuthenticationSASLContinue(salt, i)    │","  │ ◄────────────────────────────────────── │","  │  SASLResponse(ClientProof)              │","  │ ──────────────────────────────────────► │","  │  AuthenticationSASLFinal + AuthOK       │","  │ ◄────────────────────────────────────── │"]},{"type":"heading","text":"PBKDF2-SHA256 via CryptoKit","anchor":"PBKDF2-SHA256-via-CryptoKit","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SaltedPassword = Hi(password, salt, iterations)"},{"text":" derivation uses a pure Swift PBKDF2 loop over CryptoKit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HMAC<SHA256>"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var u = HMAC<SHA256>.authenticationCode(for: salt + [0,0,0,1], using: SymmetricKey(data: passwordData))","var saltedPassword = Array(u)","for _ in 1..<iterations {","    u = HMAC<SHA256>.authenticationCode(for: Data(u), using: ...)","    \/\/ XOR accumulate","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Enabling SCRAM on PostgreSQL Server","anchor":"Enabling-SCRAM-on-PostgreSQL-Server","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["-- pg_hba.conf","host  all  all  0.0.0.0\/0  scram-sha-256","","-- Verify in psql:","SELECT usename, passwd FROM pg_shadow;","-- Password should start with: SCRAM-SHA-256$4096:..."],"syntax":"sql"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Security & Performance in SwiftDatabase","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftDatabase"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/SecurityAndPerformance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftDatabase/documentation/SwiftDatabase/HighThroughputIngestion":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/HighThroughputIngestion","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/swiftdatabase\/highthroughputingestion","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Ingest millions of tabular rows into SQLite, PostgreSQL, and MySQL using zero-dependency wire protocols and batch writeback.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Bulk SQL Ingestion & Database Wire Protocols"},"doc://SwiftDatabase/documentation/SwiftDatabase/PostgreSQLConnection":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftdatabase\/postgresqlconnection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Native PostgreSQL database connection driver using PostgreSQL v3.0 wire protocol.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"PostgreSQLConnection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/PostgreSQLConnection","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostgreSQLConnection","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PostgreSQLConnection","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftDatabase/documentation/SwiftDatabase":{"abstract":[{"text":"Relational Database Connectors to DataFrames.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftdatabase","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"SwiftDatabase","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase"},"doc://SwiftDatabase/documentation/SwiftDatabase/SQLiteConnection":{"url":"\/docu